  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "The T. kivui strains were cultivated at 66 °C or 55 °C on mineral medium containing per liter: 7.80 g Na2HPO4 × 2 H2O, 6.90 g NaH2PO4 × H2O, 0.21 g K2HPO4, 0.16 g KH2PO4, 0.25 g NH4Cl, 0.225 g (NH4)2SO4, 0.448 g NaCl, 0.121 g MgSO4 × 7 H2O, 0.07 g CaCl2 × 2 H2O, 1 mL trace element solution (based on DSMZ141). The trace element solution contained per liter: 15.00 g nitrilotriacetic acid, 5.00 g MnS",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
